<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-BRAZILIAN RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZILIAN RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of weekend</p>
<p>matches in the Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro soccer</p>
<p>championships.</p>
<p>Sao Paulo championship</p>
<p> Aracatuba		   4   Juventus		    1</p>
<p> Corinthians		 5   America/S.J.Rio Preto   0</p>
<p> Internacional Limeira   2   Botafogo/Ribeirao Preto 0</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		  0   Palmeiras		   2</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista     0   Santos			2</p>
<p> Rio Branco		  2   Sao Jose		    1</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		   3   Mogi Mirim		  3</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	    0   Portuguesa		  1</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p>Group One</p>
<p> Palmeiras		 15 10  5  0 39 13 35</p>
<p> Portuguesa		15  8  5  2 34 22 29</p>
<p> Santos		    15  8  4  3 28 18 28</p>
<p> Guarani		   15  4  7  4 30 35 19</p>
<p> Juventus		  15  3  5  7 26 33 14</p>
<p> Sao Jose		  15  2  6  7 19 31 12</p>
<p> America		   15  2  3 10 11 36  9</p>
<p> Botafogo		  15  0  8  7  9 19  8</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p> Corinthians	     15  9  4  2 39 18 31</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		 15  5  8  2 23 15 23</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	  15  5  5  5 18 16 20</p>
<p>Internacional Limeira 15  5  5  5 24 25 20</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		15  5  5  5 19 21 20</p>
<p> Rio Branco		15  4  6  5 20 23 18</p>
<p> Aracatuba		 15  4  4  7 17 23 16</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista   15  4  4  7 18 26 16</p>
<p>Note: The teams play once against the other teams in their</p>
<p>own group, then twice against the teams in the other group. At</p>
<p>the end of this, the top two teams in each group qualify for</p>
<p>the final play-off stage. If teams are level on points,</p>
<p>positions are decided by the number of games won.</p>
<p>Rio de Janeiro championship, second stage</p>
<p> Bangu			1  Americano			1</p>
<p> Madureira		  1  Flamengo			 1</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama	    1  Fluminense		     0</p>
<p> Volta Redonda	    1  Botafogo			 2</p>
<p>Second stage standings</p>
<p> Botafogo		   3  2  1  0  5  3  7</p>
<p> Americano		  3  1  1  1  6  5  4</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama	    2  1  1  0  1  0  4</p>
<p> Fluminense		 3  1  1  1  3  3  4</p>
<p> Flamengo		   2  0  2  0  3  3  2</p>
<p> Bangu			2  0  2  0  1  1  2</p>
<p> Madureira		  3  0  2  1  5  7  2</p>
<p> Volta Redonda	    2  0  0  2  2  4  0</p>
<p>Note: the winners of the first, second and third stages</p>
<p>qualify for the final round. Only the top six teams in the</p>
<p>second stage carry on into the third stage. If the same team</p>
<p>wins all three stages, they become champions automatically.</p>
<p>Botafogo won the first stage.</p>
</text>
